{{!
    @template local_awareness/editor/position_option

    The label of one position radio in the notice editor: a cell of the screen the stylesheet
    draws, holding the shape the dialogue would take there. The name is carried offscreen rather
    than printed, because seven phrases describe a place where a picture of one shows it - and a
    radio with no visible text still needs its accessible name. Rendered into the radio's label by
    notice_form, which is why there is no input here.

    Context variables required for this template:
      * position - the position key, one of awareness::POSITIONS, used as a class suffix
      * name - the position's name, already a translated string
      * small - whether the dialogue drawn here is the narrow one a corner takes

    Example context (json):
    {
        "position": "top-end",
        "name": "Top end",
        "small": true
    }
}}
<span class="la-zone la-zone--{{position}}">
    <span class="la-zone-shape {{#small}}la-zone-shape--small{{/small}}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="la-offscreen">{{name}}</span>
</span>
